ating W6 is used; 2 remain unshown.\n  - T3: Previous player has a Chow T1-T2-T3, so T3 is used; 2 remain unshown.\n  - B6: Previous player has a Chow B7-B8-B9, and B6 is less connected; 4 remain unshown.\n- Among these, B6 stands out as the safest due to highest unshown count (4) and no direct adjacency to opponents' known sequences or pungs. Discarding B6 minimizes the risk of contributing to an opponent's Chow or Pung.\n\nAnswer: Play B6"}
